1
00:00:09,142 --> 00:00:14,080
Look at this cashmere.
It's 40% off. I'll save 20,000 yen.

2
00:00:15,115 --> 00:00:18,485
Akira, can I have an advance on my salary?

3
00:00:18,551 --> 00:00:19,452
Sure.

4
00:00:20,854 --> 00:00:22,255
You're so generous today.

5
00:00:22,522 --> 00:00:26,493
Shopping is about ambition.
Raise your ambitions with this,

6
00:00:26,559 --> 00:00:28,528
do many operations, and earn money.

7
00:00:28,595 --> 00:00:30,730
Shopping is ambition? Yes sir!

8
00:00:30,797 --> 00:00:33,533
- Let's go for a fitting spree.
- This and that.

9
00:00:33,600 --> 00:00:36,636
I apologize.
Another customer is using the room.

10
00:00:37,003 --> 00:00:40,240
Nice, nice. I love it.

11
00:00:40,306 --> 00:00:42,142
It suits you perfectly.

12
00:00:42,342 --> 00:00:46,379
I'll take everything from here
to there in different colors.

13
00:00:46,446 --> 00:00:48,748
Thanks as always, Mr. Ninomiya.

14
00:00:49,749 --> 00:00:54,854
I don't want cheap people like them
to wear the same brand as me.

15
00:00:54,921 --> 00:00:55,755
Here.

16
00:00:56,656 --> 00:01:01,027
Who wants to wear the same brand
with that lame old man?

17
00:01:01,428 --> 00:01:04,030
If you don't want it, I'll take it.

18
00:01:04,097 --> 00:01:07,434
Not this one. It won't suit you.

19
00:01:07,500 --> 00:01:08,334
Don't pull. Ouch.

20
00:01:15,708 --> 00:01:16,609
Oh my gosh.

21
00:01:22,749 --> 00:01:25,652
What is your relationship
with the professor?

22
00:01:25,919 --> 00:01:29,189
Tamao, you're misunderstanding.

23
00:01:30,623 --> 00:01:33,426
Did you, by any chance,
buy it at the sale too?

24
00:01:33,560 --> 00:01:35,895
You mean like a bargain sale?

25
00:01:37,130 --> 00:01:38,698
You're so funny.

26
00:01:39,766 --> 00:01:42,202
You think I would go there?

27
00:01:42,368 --> 00:01:45,105
My patient gave this as a present.

28
00:01:49,042 --> 00:01:50,009
What are you looking at?

29
00:01:50,910 --> 00:01:51,744
Nothing.

30
00:01:52,178 --> 00:01:55,181
Please forgive me for misbehaving.

31
00:01:55,648 --> 00:01:56,516
Shall we go?

32
00:02:09,662 --> 00:02:13,266
- Are you being readmitted?
- I just need some rest.

33
00:02:13,333 --> 00:02:15,401
What do you mean by "rest"?

34
00:02:20,406 --> 00:02:24,144
I said this is a hospital!

35
00:02:25,845 --> 00:02:28,882
Thanks for choosing us
for your examination,

36
00:02:28,948 --> 00:02:30,617
Mr. Ninomiya.

37
00:02:30,683 --> 00:02:32,986
Is my usual room available?

38
00:02:33,052 --> 00:02:36,389
We've prepared
the best room for you.

39
00:02:36,456 --> 00:02:38,057
How have you been, sir?

40
00:02:38,124 --> 00:02:41,661
I'm not worried
about my illness one bit.

41
00:02:41,728 --> 00:02:46,566
I know I had the best doctor
for my surgery.

42
00:02:46,633 --> 00:02:49,869
Our executive manager Hiruma
will pay you a visit later.

43
00:02:51,471 --> 00:02:52,539
Too many matching ones.

44
00:02:53,540 --> 00:02:56,075
I can't stand wearing pairs
with those lame old men.

45
00:02:56,643 --> 00:02:57,777
I shouldn't have bought it.

46
00:03:08,288 --> 00:03:12,525
- What's this, Dr. Daimon?
- I don't need it. I made a bad purchase.

47
00:03:12,992 --> 00:03:14,227
Bad purchase?

48
00:03:23,870 --> 00:03:26,739
KAZUYO MABUCHI, EXECUTIVE MANAGER
INTERNAL MEDICINE

49
00:03:27,373 --> 00:03:30,510
This is a story
about a maverick female doctor.

50
00:03:34,447 --> 00:03:37,550
<i>Executive manager</i>
<i>of the surgery department Hiruma</i>

51
00:03:38,117 --> 00:03:41,087
<i>will make rounds</i>
<i>in the 2nd surgery department.</i>

52
00:03:41,688 --> 00:03:47,327
<i>Offices in university hospitals</i>
<i>have lost their authorities.</i>

53
00:03:47,660 --> 00:03:50,430
<i>It's entered into the law of jungle.</i>

54
00:03:51,264 --> 00:03:54,467
<i>To save this crisis</i>
<i>in the world of medical care,</i>

55
00:03:54,534 --> 00:03:59,339
<i>a freelance doctor, in other words,</i>
<i>a maverick doctor appeared.</i>

56
00:04:00,406 --> 00:04:01,574
Get in line at the very end.

57
00:04:02,141 --> 00:04:03,743
- Daimon!
- I won't do that.

58
00:04:06,746 --> 00:04:09,549
Tell me the reason, Daimon.

59
00:04:10,817 --> 00:04:12,252
Answer the executive manager.

60
00:04:12,485 --> 00:04:13,486
Because it's useless.

61
00:04:14,053 --> 00:04:14,887
Useless?

62
00:04:16,122 --> 00:04:18,224
A grand procession in the hospital

63
00:04:18,658 --> 00:04:22,695
is a custom where an inept professor
shows off his authority.

64
00:04:23,830 --> 00:04:25,832
It's a lot of nuisance to patients.

65
00:04:28,134 --> 00:04:32,472
Daimon,
you don't understand anything.

66
00:04:32,639 --> 00:04:37,644
Our patients appreciate the brand
of Teito Medical University Hospital

67
00:04:38,111 --> 00:04:41,180
and our organizational capabilities.

68
00:04:41,681 --> 00:04:44,517
That's why they entrust us
with their treatments.

69
00:04:45,852 --> 00:04:51,491
Our rounds are, so to speak,
a ceremony to express our response

70
00:04:51,858 --> 00:04:55,561
to the trust and expectations
our patients have given us.

71
00:04:56,195 --> 00:04:57,030
Yes, sir.

72
00:04:58,765 --> 00:05:00,933
Understood? Get in the back.

73
00:05:01,668 --> 00:05:02,635
I won't do that.

74
00:05:03,102 --> 00:05:05,405
<i>For example, this woman.</i>

75
00:05:05,938 --> 00:05:09,709
<i>She hates groups, authority,</i>
<i>and being controlled.</i>

76
00:05:10,510 --> 00:05:15,648
<i>Her medical certifications</i>
<i>and work experience are her only weapons.</i>

77
00:05:16,349 --> 00:05:22,055
<i>Surgeon Michiko Daimon,</i>
<i>also known as Doctor-X.</i>

78
00:05:47,747 --> 00:05:50,950
Your attitude
for giving attention to each knot

79
00:05:51,217 --> 00:05:53,786
will show your sincerity as a surgeon.

80
00:05:53,853 --> 00:05:54,987
Yes.

81
00:05:57,256 --> 00:05:59,525
Isn't there any patient
I can operate on immediately?

82
00:06:04,163 --> 00:06:06,666
Here come my withdrawal symptoms.

83
00:06:09,168 --> 00:06:10,536
Are you an alcoholic?

84
00:06:10,603 --> 00:06:14,140
Without a scalpel, my hands start shaking.

85
00:06:25,918 --> 00:06:27,286
- A recurrence?
- Yes.

86
00:06:27,487 --> 00:06:28,654
That can't be.

87
00:06:29,122 --> 00:06:31,324
It must be some kind of a mistake.

88
00:06:31,424 --> 00:06:33,326
It's not a mistake.

89
00:06:33,659 --> 00:06:37,697
It's a recurrence
of ascending colon cancer.

90
00:06:39,198 --> 00:06:40,233
I don't believe it.

91
00:06:42,101 --> 00:06:46,606
Care for words. He's the president
of Ninomiya Real Estate.

92
00:06:46,672 --> 00:06:47,673
You're lying!

93
00:06:47,874 --> 00:06:50,510
The highest ranking professor
operated on me

94
00:06:50,810 --> 00:06:53,379
in Teito Medical University Hospital.

95
00:06:53,713 --> 00:06:58,885
I know Professor Hiruma
performed your surgery this January.

96
00:06:58,951 --> 00:07:00,920
He said the surgery was a success

97
00:07:00,987 --> 00:07:04,624
and that the cancer was
completely removed.

98
00:07:05,091 --> 00:07:07,059
I gave him a lot for a reward.

99
00:07:07,193 --> 00:07:11,864
Five million yen with a scarf!
I paid five million yen in cash!

100
00:07:12,198 --> 00:07:13,366
Really?

101
00:07:13,499 --> 00:07:16,335
A recurrence? That's bullshit!

102
00:07:16,402 --> 00:07:18,271
I won't believe you.

103
00:07:18,404 --> 00:07:19,572
Call Hiruma!

104
00:07:19,972 --> 00:07:24,076
We'll discuss about our treatment plan
when you are calm.

105
00:07:24,310 --> 00:07:26,879
This is a problem. I'm in trouble.

106
00:07:28,481 --> 00:07:33,453
He donates a considerable amount
to our surgery dept. Every year.

107
00:07:33,519 --> 00:07:37,390
He is an important cash source...
Excuse me, a patient to us.

108
00:07:37,657 --> 00:07:39,459
That's right.

109
00:07:40,660 --> 00:07:42,995
He's also a relative of my wife.

110
00:07:46,999 --> 00:07:49,335
Why now?

111
00:07:50,536 --> 00:07:52,104
Such bad timing.

112
00:07:52,338 --> 00:07:57,276
The chairperson election
that costs so much money is coming.

113
00:07:57,677 --> 00:08:00,580
I'm bored to death.
Please let me do surgery.

114
00:08:01,614 --> 00:08:02,582
Knock when you come in.

115
00:08:11,791 --> 00:08:13,426
Recurrence of the anastomotic part?

116
00:08:14,060 --> 00:08:15,361
Let me do the operation.

117
00:08:16,596 --> 00:08:17,630
It's not a recurrence.

118
00:08:17,697 --> 00:08:18,865
How terrible.

119
00:08:18,931 --> 00:08:20,700
This is a recurrence.

120
00:08:20,833 --> 00:08:22,602
Please wait, Mr. Ninomiya.

121
00:08:22,668 --> 00:08:24,570
- Professor.
- Let me go.

122
00:08:24,837 --> 00:08:26,873
He's in an important meeting.

123
00:08:27,006 --> 00:08:29,942
It's not a recurrence, is it?

124
00:08:30,009 --> 00:08:32,345
You performed the operation.

125
00:08:32,478 --> 00:08:34,480
Tell me it's not.

126
00:08:34,680 --> 00:08:35,882
Of course, it's not.

127
00:08:37,350 --> 00:08:39,318
Who told you such a thing?

128
00:08:39,452 --> 00:08:41,854
The executive manager
of internal medicine.

129
00:08:43,589 --> 00:08:45,091
Professor Mabuchi?

130
00:08:45,658 --> 00:08:49,328
She is pretty,

131
00:08:49,829 --> 00:08:52,832
but she's rather pessimistic.

132
00:08:53,666 --> 00:08:57,136
She's most afraid
of lawsuits from the patients.

133
00:08:57,203 --> 00:08:59,672
Then there's no recurrence?

134
00:08:59,805 --> 00:09:01,908
Of course not.

135
00:09:02,275 --> 00:09:05,545
Don't worry.
I was with him as the 1st assistant

136
00:09:05,945 --> 00:09:08,047
and his operation was perfect.

137
00:09:08,848 --> 00:09:10,449
I was his second assistant.

138
00:09:10,650 --> 00:09:13,486
He was very precise
and recurrence is impossible.

139
00:09:14,153 --> 00:09:15,121
Mr. Ninomiya.

140
00:09:15,555 --> 00:09:20,693
All cancer experts here agree
that there was no mistake.

141
00:09:25,064 --> 00:09:28,801
That's true. I'm so glad.

142
00:09:31,537 --> 00:09:32,805
However, Mr. Ninomiya,

143
00:09:33,105 --> 00:09:37,443
we found a tiny new cancer

144
00:09:37,610 --> 00:09:40,746
which is completely different
from the last one.

145
00:09:40,846 --> 00:09:42,782
Let's remove it as soon as we can.

146
00:09:42,982 --> 00:09:44,850
A new cancer?

147
00:09:44,917 --> 00:09:47,853
It's early stage 1.
Don't worry.

148
00:09:47,987 --> 00:09:49,288
And of course,

149
00:09:50,556 --> 00:09:52,625
I will perform the surgery like last time.

150
00:09:53,192 --> 00:09:57,229
I see.
I will rely on you completely.

151
00:09:58,731 --> 00:10:02,134
- Take good care of me.
- Don't worry.

152
00:10:02,902 --> 00:10:06,572
You're in good hands.
There is nothing to worry about.

153
00:10:09,108 --> 00:10:12,378
Hiruma is more passionate
about the election than surgery.

154
00:10:12,511 --> 00:10:13,379
Why?

155
00:10:13,646 --> 00:10:16,248
Because his beloved
bundle of cash comes and goes.

156
00:10:16,716 --> 00:10:19,752
Let's say, one vote
from a professor is one million.

157
00:10:20,553 --> 00:10:24,090
Fifty of them will make 50 million yen.

158
00:10:28,394 --> 00:10:32,632
This is for the donation
and this for Prof. Hiruma.

159
00:10:32,698 --> 00:10:36,535
President Ninomiya
is Hiruma's patron.

160
00:10:36,736 --> 00:10:37,570
Patron?

161
00:10:37,703 --> 00:10:39,405
He's a big source of cash.

162
00:10:39,605 --> 00:10:44,110
So he's desperate to
erase the fact that cancer recurred.

163
00:10:44,176 --> 00:10:46,145
A big source of cash.

164
00:10:46,579 --> 00:10:49,982
I envy him. I wish I had one too.

165
00:10:50,049 --> 00:10:51,884
That's impossible for you, Daimon.

166
00:10:54,453 --> 00:10:55,321
You startled me.

167
00:10:55,621 --> 00:10:57,423
Jonouchi, you were here?

168
00:10:57,657 --> 00:10:58,858
At Yasuda Hospital.

169
00:10:59,158 --> 00:11:02,862
The surgeon was so slow
that it took three hours longer.

170
00:11:02,928 --> 00:11:06,032
I've got it.
I'll charge for overtime.

171
00:11:06,098 --> 00:11:07,233
Thank you.

172
00:11:08,267 --> 00:11:09,769
Why can't I have a patron?

173
00:11:09,902 --> 00:11:12,838
No patron will benefit
from spending money

174
00:11:12,905 --> 00:11:15,041
on someone beyond control.

175
00:11:15,241 --> 00:11:16,075
That's correct.

176
00:11:16,342 --> 00:11:20,179
But it's suspicious
if Hiruma operated on him.

177
00:11:20,279 --> 00:11:22,548
He's only present at the beginning,

178
00:11:22,648 --> 00:11:25,951
leaves the rest to his staff
and disappears for golf or the gym,

179
00:11:26,018 --> 00:11:28,754
or goes out with women.

180
00:11:29,155 --> 00:11:32,558
The more authority one has,
the less time one stays.

181
00:11:33,125 --> 00:11:36,662
Chun-Kan! That's the third one.

182
00:11:37,463 --> 00:11:40,232
I anticipate that his subordinates

183
00:11:40,299 --> 00:11:43,769
will sacrifice themselves
to protect Hiruma.

184
00:11:43,836 --> 00:11:44,870
Why would they do that?

185
00:11:45,071 --> 00:11:49,742
He'll then be indebted to them
and help them win in the election.

186
00:11:50,076 --> 00:11:51,877
I'm getting more confused.

187
00:11:51,944 --> 00:11:55,347
That's why the worse ones get ahead
in a university hospital.

188
00:11:55,414 --> 00:11:56,282
That's right.

189
00:11:56,682 --> 00:11:58,884
Why don't you play with us?

190
00:11:59,118 --> 00:12:02,254
I have to pick up my kid
from the overtime day care.

191
00:12:04,190 --> 00:12:08,327
I feel sorry for a single parent.
Bye-bye.

192
00:12:08,961 --> 00:12:10,329
I feel sorry for you too, Michiko.

193
00:12:10,396 --> 00:12:11,931
- Why?
- Kan!

194
00:12:17,436 --> 00:12:18,270
Yakuman!

195
00:12:35,421 --> 00:12:36,355
I'm home.

196
00:12:36,922 --> 00:12:37,757
Oh, honey!

197
00:12:38,290 --> 00:12:40,359
You're home early.

198
00:12:41,861 --> 00:12:44,063
Welcome,
ladies from the Shirobara Club.

199
00:12:44,330 --> 00:12:46,432
Welcome back, Executive Manager.

200
00:12:46,499 --> 00:12:48,200
Thanks for having us.

201
00:12:48,334 --> 00:12:50,636
Please enjoy yourselves.

202
00:12:50,703 --> 00:12:52,404
Thank you.

203
00:12:52,772 --> 00:12:54,073
Wait a second, honey.

204
00:12:55,975 --> 00:12:59,078
I heard Uncle Ninomiya has
an operation again.

205
00:13:00,012 --> 00:13:01,747
You're quick to get the news.

206
00:13:01,814 --> 00:13:03,582
I got a call from my aunt.

207
00:13:04,183 --> 00:13:09,288
She thinks that you made a mistake
in the last operation.

208
00:13:10,456 --> 00:13:11,357
No way.

209
00:13:11,490 --> 00:13:12,892
How awful, isn't it?

210
00:13:13,692 --> 00:13:17,997
I told her my husband, the executive
manager of the surgery dept.,

211
00:13:18,063 --> 00:13:19,198
would never make mistakes.

212
00:13:19,598 --> 00:13:23,469
My husband always tells me
you're the treasure of our hospital.

213
00:13:23,536 --> 00:13:28,140
My husband is honored to assist you
during your operation.

214
00:13:28,207 --> 00:13:29,575
That's nice of him to say.

215
00:13:30,676 --> 00:13:32,144
Yukako isn't home yet?

216
00:13:32,411 --> 00:13:34,113
She's out with her friends.

217
00:13:34,180 --> 00:13:38,851
By the way, Mrs. Ebina suggested
Dr. Kondo for Yukako.

218
00:13:39,618 --> 00:13:40,452
Kondo?

219
00:13:40,586 --> 00:13:43,322
He joined your team last year.

220
00:13:43,489 --> 00:13:45,991
He is tall and handsome.

221
00:13:46,058 --> 00:13:49,261
Unlike me,
Yukako loves good looking men.

222
00:13:49,728 --> 00:13:52,798
The most handsome surgeon?

223
00:13:52,998 --> 00:13:54,500
What is Dr. Kondo like?

224
00:13:54,567 --> 00:13:57,503
Indeed he is handsome.

225
00:13:58,070 --> 00:14:00,973
But he didn't graduate
from Teito Medical University.

226
00:14:01,173 --> 00:14:04,977
He went to
a local national university

227
00:14:05,110 --> 00:14:07,947
so he's considered
off the career track.

228
00:14:10,149 --> 00:14:12,852
I'm sorry. I didn't know.

229
00:14:12,985 --> 00:14:15,788
I'd like to see him
if he's that handsome.

230
00:14:16,021 --> 00:14:19,792
Not as a candidate for my son-in-law,
but as my eye candy.

231
00:14:22,795 --> 00:14:28,200
We have better wines in the cellar
that you got from your uncle.

232
00:14:28,300 --> 00:14:29,368
Why don't you serve them?

233
00:14:39,378 --> 00:14:42,448
Hula dancing in
the autumn night?

234
00:14:43,115 --> 00:14:44,250
What idiots.

235
00:14:45,484 --> 00:14:49,922
Hiruma intends to do the surgery,

236
00:14:50,823 --> 00:14:52,925
but what do you think, Kondo?

237
00:14:53,425 --> 00:14:54,860
He shouldn't do it.

238
00:14:55,427 --> 00:14:57,563
There is a chance it may spread.

239
00:14:57,863 --> 00:15:00,933
If the cancer has spread
to the peritoneum,

240
00:15:01,000 --> 00:15:02,401
there is nothing we can do.

241
00:15:03,969 --> 00:15:10,876
How about an open surgery,
inviting the board members and all?

242
00:15:14,847 --> 00:15:18,484
We should show everyone
when Hiruma is cornered.

243
00:15:18,550 --> 00:15:21,186
The Hiruma Brand will
collapse instantly.

244
00:15:28,294 --> 00:15:32,665
Don't look at me like that.

245
00:15:38,170 --> 00:15:43,108
That scarf doesn't suit you.
Can I have it?

246
00:15:46,078 --> 00:15:46,912
Sure.

247
00:15:48,280 --> 00:15:51,216
That freelance surgeon
that I invited...

248
00:15:51,784 --> 00:15:53,819
Was her name Michiko Daimon?

249
00:15:54,853 --> 00:15:59,391
Don't take interest in
a no-brand woman like her.

250
00:16:13,605 --> 00:16:18,210
The first case is a 65-year-old male,
Mr. Kinya Ninomiya.

251
00:16:19,178 --> 00:16:20,312
In January this year,

252
00:16:20,379 --> 00:16:23,148
he removed
an ascending colon cancer here.

253
00:16:23,449 --> 00:16:25,617
A tumor was found
two days ago during check-up.

254
00:16:25,951 --> 00:16:28,887
A 3-cm lesion was detected
at the anastomotic part.

255
00:16:29,054 --> 00:16:32,224
Cancer recurrence can be
highly possible...

256
00:16:32,291 --> 00:16:34,393
Be careful with your statement.

257
00:16:34,626 --> 00:16:36,662
- Take it back.
- Please forgive me, sir.

258
00:16:36,895 --> 00:16:41,066
I believe the previous operation
by Prof. Hiruma was perfect.

259
00:16:41,700 --> 00:16:45,270
But I guess there are people
in internal medicine

260
00:16:45,704 --> 00:16:48,807
who suspect recurrence, right?

261
00:16:49,942 --> 00:16:52,578
Yes, it seems like it.

262
00:16:59,885 --> 00:17:00,753
What is it?

263
00:17:03,322 --> 00:17:08,127
Should there be any possibility
of recurrence, it is my fault.

264
00:17:08,494 --> 00:17:09,795
Please forgive me, sir.

265
00:17:11,330 --> 00:17:12,798
During the operation in January,

266
00:17:13,432 --> 00:17:17,102
you had to stop the operation
due to an emergency.

267
00:17:17,903 --> 00:17:20,572
I believe
I made a mistake after I took over.

268
00:17:21,173 --> 00:17:22,074
I don't think so.

269
00:17:22,808 --> 00:17:23,709
Sir!

270
00:17:25,744 --> 00:17:28,514
I decided
the extent of the removal part.

271
00:17:28,680 --> 00:17:31,417
I made a mistake in my judgment.
It is my fault.

272
00:17:31,617 --> 00:17:34,820
- It is my mistake.
- Akira was right.

273
00:17:34,953 --> 00:17:36,422
Ebina and Kameyama.

274
00:17:37,389 --> 00:17:39,892
I understand how you feel.
Return to your seats.

275
00:17:48,067 --> 00:17:52,071
I hate to have to say this.

276
00:17:53,205 --> 00:17:58,944
We, surgeons, should not be swayed
by the doctors in internal medicine.

277
00:17:59,878 --> 00:18:02,681
As the executive manager
of the surgery department,

278
00:18:03,248 --> 00:18:08,253
I declare that
this is not a recurrence.

279
00:18:09,321 --> 00:18:13,926
But there is a possibility

280
00:18:15,294 --> 00:18:19,064
that a totally new cancer may occur...

281
00:18:30,709 --> 00:18:32,544
Small ascites.

282
00:18:32,811 --> 00:18:33,779
Ascites?

283
00:18:35,614 --> 00:18:41,386
I'll perform the operation.
Reserve the operating room tomorrow.

284
00:18:42,521 --> 00:18:46,625
- Ebina and Kameyama, be ready...
- Before that,

285
00:18:48,694 --> 00:18:50,996
I suggest you to conduct PET-CT.

286
00:18:51,630 --> 00:18:52,664
It is not necessary.

287
00:18:53,599 --> 00:18:54,733
Will you be inconvenienced

288
00:18:55,934 --> 00:19:00,239
if we were assured
of the recurrence from the CT?

289
00:19:08,447 --> 00:19:09,982
Inconvenienced?

290
00:19:14,153 --> 00:19:18,257
You are so funny, Daimon.

291
00:19:20,125 --> 00:19:24,396
If that's what you want,
we'll add PET-CT.

292
00:19:25,597 --> 00:19:29,601
I don't want to
be unjustly suspected either.

293
00:19:35,908 --> 00:19:37,009
Thank you.

294
00:19:37,409 --> 00:19:38,243
Alright.

295
00:19:51,757 --> 00:19:53,392
<i>Here's a quick note.</i>

296
00:19:53,892 --> 00:19:56,395
<i>We found peritoneal dissemination</i>

297
00:19:57,029 --> 00:19:58,564
<i>in the patient from PET-CT.</i>

298
00:19:59,264 --> 00:20:00,098
<i>From Kondo.</i>

299
00:20:06,638 --> 00:20:09,141
You found peritoneal dissemination?

300
00:20:09,741 --> 00:20:11,944
- Yes.
- We're in trouble.

301
00:20:13,946 --> 00:20:14,913
Just as I thought.

302
00:20:17,849 --> 00:20:19,251
This is serious.

303
00:20:19,585 --> 00:20:23,121
With this range,
surgical approach is impossible.

304
00:20:32,497 --> 00:20:35,000
What brings you here, Prof. Mabuchi?

305
00:20:35,968 --> 00:20:39,705
I see all the doctors
from internal medicine.

306
00:20:40,439 --> 00:20:43,575
Our department will take care
of Mr. Kinya Ninomiya.

307
00:20:44,476 --> 00:20:46,111
What is this all of a sudden?

308
00:20:47,446 --> 00:20:50,749
Peritoneal dissemination can't be
treated by surgery.

309
00:20:52,150 --> 00:20:53,652
Who said such a thing?

310
00:20:53,785 --> 00:20:57,222
Anyway, please hand him to
internal medicine.

311
00:20:57,289 --> 00:20:58,590
We can handle it.

312
00:21:00,025 --> 00:21:01,860
You must be kidding.

313
00:21:02,361 --> 00:21:04,630
Mr. Ninomiya is my patient.

314
00:21:05,497 --> 00:21:07,099
Stay out of this issue.

315
00:21:07,232 --> 00:21:11,169
We are offering help
for your emergency.

316
00:21:11,370 --> 00:21:14,806
FOLFOX treatment proves to
be very effective

317
00:21:15,474 --> 00:21:16,942
in prolonging life in such cases.

318
00:21:17,676 --> 00:21:22,514
This treatment has prolonged lives
to nearly two years

319
00:21:22,581 --> 00:21:25,350
from an average of one year
in other treatments.

320
00:21:25,851 --> 00:21:28,954
You're just citing data,
but you can't cure the disease.

321
00:21:29,087 --> 00:21:33,725
This treatment is effective to those
who cannot be operated on.

322
00:21:33,792 --> 00:21:34,826
Wait a second.

323
00:21:35,994 --> 00:21:40,198
I am the one who decides
if surgery is possible or not.

324
00:21:40,265 --> 00:21:41,800
Yes, sir.

325
00:21:42,701 --> 00:21:45,737
Are you considering surgery?

326
00:21:45,871 --> 00:21:47,773
- Of course.
- I'm dumbfounded.

327
00:21:48,073 --> 00:21:50,575
What you're trying to protect

328
00:21:50,842 --> 00:21:54,780
is not your patient's life,
but your own brand name.

329
00:21:56,081 --> 00:21:57,616
It's nonsense.

330
00:21:57,683 --> 00:22:02,487
The images show the peritoneal
dissemination area is too large.

331
00:22:02,654 --> 00:22:06,825
Removal of the primary lesion and
peritoneal dissemination is absurd.

332
00:22:07,159 --> 00:22:08,794
- Yes, ma'am.
- Yes, ma'am.

333
00:22:08,860 --> 00:22:12,931
- You all shut up.
- Cool down.

334
00:22:13,665 --> 00:22:18,203
Are you sure you want to
kill your valuable sponsor?

335
00:22:19,304 --> 00:22:21,340
You'll not only damage your career,

336
00:22:22,507 --> 00:22:24,976
but you'll be sued by the family.

337
00:22:26,812 --> 00:22:33,118
Nobody would be willing to do
such a risky operation.

338
00:22:33,952 --> 00:22:35,287
I could do it.

339
00:22:36,221 --> 00:22:37,189
Who are you?

340
00:22:38,190 --> 00:22:40,859
Michiko Daimon, who never fails.

341
00:22:40,992 --> 00:22:42,894
You're just a part-timer.

342
00:22:42,961 --> 00:22:44,763
Who do you think you are?

343
00:22:59,344 --> 00:23:00,379
KANBARA DOCTOR AGENCY

344
00:23:00,445 --> 00:23:03,081
Why do they want to talk to me?

345
00:23:04,015 --> 00:23:05,951
Did Michiko do something again?

346
00:23:07,052 --> 00:23:09,287
Please have a seat.

347
00:23:12,290 --> 00:23:13,992
Does he mean on this?

348
00:23:16,828 --> 00:23:19,831
You don't have to sit.

349
00:23:19,898 --> 00:23:21,733
Please have some green tea.

350
00:23:21,967 --> 00:23:23,034
Don't trouble yourself.

351
00:23:24,202 --> 00:23:28,740
Our executive manager only
drinks black tea.

352
00:23:34,713 --> 00:23:37,783
Is Daimon fired already?

353
00:23:37,916 --> 00:23:39,985
Not for now.

354
00:23:40,118 --> 00:23:41,253
I see.

355
00:23:42,721 --> 00:23:43,688
I'm relieved.

356
00:23:44,089 --> 00:23:49,027
- Is she fired that often?
- Yes.

357
00:23:49,327 --> 00:23:52,264
Once Michiko Daimon enters
the operating room,

358
00:23:52,631 --> 00:23:55,700
she goes headlong to
whatever she sets her mind to.

359
00:23:56,568 --> 00:23:58,503
She never turns back.

360
00:24:00,238 --> 00:24:04,409
Once a surgery starts, she sees
only the organs of the patient.

361
00:24:06,178 --> 00:24:09,781
- Then she got fired before?
- Yes.

362
00:24:13,452 --> 00:24:14,986
What can I do for you today?

363
00:24:15,454 --> 00:24:22,427
I'm here as the executive manager
of the surgery department.

364
00:24:24,496 --> 00:24:27,032
I'm visiting the home of our newcomer.

365
00:24:29,901 --> 00:24:33,205
I couldn't do
any operations today either.

366
00:24:37,876 --> 00:24:38,844
What's wrong?

367
00:24:39,411 --> 00:24:41,046
It's five o'clock. I'm leaving.

368
00:24:41,413 --> 00:24:44,216
Professor Hiruma wants
to see you, Daimon.

369
00:24:44,683 --> 00:24:47,919
- I don't work overtime.
- Just come.

370
00:24:49,287 --> 00:24:50,121
Excuse us.

371
00:24:52,791 --> 00:24:53,792
Thanks for waiting.

372
00:24:58,063 --> 00:25:03,735
From 8 o'clock tomorrow morning,
we'll perform Ninomiya's surgery.

373
00:25:04,803 --> 00:25:05,670
Don't be late.

374
00:25:07,272 --> 00:25:08,773
You'll let me take charge?

375
00:25:09,007 --> 00:25:10,075
Are you kidding?

376
00:25:11,109 --> 00:25:13,411
You're my fourth assistant.

377
00:25:14,112 --> 00:25:16,448
- Assistant? Dang it.
- What do you mean?

378
00:25:16,515 --> 00:25:20,519
Is that all? Assistant, huh?

379
00:25:26,491 --> 00:25:29,461
Prof. Hiruma,
why did you choose her?

380
00:25:30,328 --> 00:25:31,363
I'd like to know why.

381
00:25:31,630 --> 00:25:34,766
I also need your help tomorrow.

382
00:25:36,868 --> 00:25:42,807
No matter how risky the surgery is,
we must confront it.

383
00:25:43,008 --> 00:25:46,444
It is our mission as surgeons.

384
00:25:47,646 --> 00:25:48,480
Yes, sir.

385
00:25:56,755 --> 00:25:58,657
I can't stand it.

386
00:25:58,857 --> 00:26:01,660
Cheer up. You can operate tomorrow.

387
00:26:01,960 --> 00:26:05,664
I'm the fourth assistant.
I can't grab a scalpel.

388
00:26:05,730 --> 00:26:09,334
- You never know what will happen.
- I know that.

389
00:26:09,634 --> 00:26:11,770
Have a conference with me?

390
00:26:12,003 --> 00:26:13,138
For tomorrow's operation?

391
00:26:13,204 --> 00:26:15,073
That's right. A dancing conference.

392
00:26:15,407 --> 00:26:16,675
Conference!

393
00:26:57,515 --> 00:26:59,284
You're late, Miss Fourth Assistant.

394
00:26:59,584 --> 00:27:01,620
We still have 5 seconds. We're okay.

395
00:27:01,820 --> 00:27:03,221
You lack tension.

396
00:27:03,288 --> 00:27:05,223
I danced too much last night.

397
00:27:05,290 --> 00:27:06,725
Dance the rest of your life.

398
00:27:06,858 --> 00:27:08,326
Professor Hiruma is late.

399
00:27:18,903 --> 00:27:20,805
That spot is for Professor Hiruma.

400
00:27:21,606 --> 00:27:23,908
The fourth assistant should be here.

401
00:27:24,109 --> 00:27:24,943
It was just a habit.

402
00:27:26,144 --> 00:27:27,012
We apologize.

403
00:27:33,084 --> 00:27:34,185
Shall we begin?

404
00:27:34,986 --> 00:27:39,457
We now begin Mr. Ninomiya's surgery
to remove ascending colon cancer.

405
00:27:39,524 --> 00:27:40,458
Scalpel.

406
00:27:48,266 --> 00:27:50,335
How impressive your scalpel skill.

407
00:27:50,869 --> 00:27:51,903
It's outstanding.

408
00:28:07,719 --> 00:28:08,820
Wipe my sweat.

409
00:28:08,887 --> 00:28:10,522
Sure. Excuse me.

410
00:28:19,497 --> 00:28:20,331
Monopolar.

411
00:28:30,442 --> 00:28:33,511
- There's a great deal of adhesion.
- I agree, sir.

412
00:28:34,079 --> 00:28:37,882
Professor Hiruma looks
unusually tense today.

413
00:28:38,550 --> 00:28:41,486
Is the operation that difficult?

414
00:28:41,619 --> 00:28:43,988
The success rate is below 5%.

415
00:28:44,522 --> 00:28:47,592
I feel sorry for the patient.

416
00:28:48,760 --> 00:28:51,863
- This is so reckless.
- Oh my!

417
00:28:57,669 --> 00:29:01,206
We'll reach the primary lesion
of the ascending colon.

418
00:29:01,806 --> 00:29:04,075
I see fluid in the intraperitoneal cavity.

419
00:29:04,209 --> 00:29:07,212
- As I expected.
- It's not much. It should be fine.

420
00:29:13,785 --> 00:29:14,786
My goodness.

421
00:29:17,222 --> 00:29:18,923
Peritoneal dissemination!

422
00:29:18,990 --> 00:29:20,692
It's all over.

423
00:29:20,825 --> 00:29:25,430
Dissemination from mesenteric
membrane to subphrenic peritoneum.

424
00:29:26,131 --> 00:29:28,333
It's beyond my expectation.

425
00:29:28,399 --> 00:29:29,868
Just as I expected.

426
00:29:30,068 --> 00:29:32,070
What happened? An emergency?

427
00:29:33,404 --> 00:29:35,340
It's worse than we expected.

428
00:29:36,307 --> 00:29:39,210
This may be the worst case scenario.

429
00:29:41,412 --> 00:29:44,949
It means that
the success rate is close to zero.

430
00:29:45,083 --> 00:29:48,453
Zero? That's bad.

431
00:29:48,720 --> 00:29:51,723
Please do your best, Prof. Hiruma.

432
00:29:55,360 --> 00:29:56,327
Professor Hiruma.

433
00:30:01,533 --> 00:30:05,336
It's impossible to remove

434
00:30:06,070 --> 00:30:11,509
such a widespread
peritoneal dissemination.

435
00:30:13,211 --> 00:30:16,247
It's very unfortunate,
but it's inoperable.

436
00:30:16,548 --> 00:30:18,016
- You're kidding.
- Yes, sir.

437
00:30:18,082 --> 00:30:19,050
It's very unfortunate.

438
00:30:23,254 --> 00:30:27,659
Are they going to close it
without removing the bad part?

439
00:30:27,792 --> 00:30:31,529
That's why I warned them
and told them to hand it to us.

440
00:30:31,663 --> 00:30:33,731
Why did you open him
in the first place?

441
00:30:41,472 --> 00:30:43,508
- Can you move?
- Don't push me.

442
00:30:43,575 --> 00:30:45,243
- Are you okay, sir?
- What are you doing?

443
00:30:46,945 --> 00:30:52,784
We have no choice, but to hand
the patient to internal medicine.

444
00:30:55,620 --> 00:30:57,655
We need to send him there.

445
00:31:07,131 --> 00:31:09,234
Michiko Daimon, the fourth assistant.

446
00:31:10,368 --> 00:31:14,706
You are responsible for closing him up.

447
00:31:16,474 --> 00:31:17,308
Understood?

448
00:31:26,251 --> 00:31:28,720
Both the first and second assistants
left too.

449
00:31:29,587 --> 00:31:32,257
What are you going to do?

450
00:31:32,991 --> 00:31:33,825
Monopolar.

451
00:31:34,826 --> 00:31:35,960
What are you going to do?

452
00:31:36,227 --> 00:31:38,897
Remove the primary lesion
and the entire peritoneum.

453
00:31:39,163 --> 00:31:40,899
Remove the entire peritoneum?

454
00:31:41,399 --> 00:31:45,536
- Too much burden on the patient.
- He's right. Stop it.

455
00:31:46,137 --> 00:31:49,073
You don't have to barge in this time.

456
00:31:49,173 --> 00:31:51,876
Internal medicine will do the rest.

457
00:31:52,010 --> 00:31:52,911
I can do it.

458
00:31:53,311 --> 00:31:54,178
Stop it!

459
00:31:56,447 --> 00:31:58,683
There is a high risk of complication,

460
00:31:59,183 --> 00:32:01,286
and he may die during the surgery.

461
00:32:01,419 --> 00:32:04,589
Oh, no! Stop it!

462
00:32:06,124 --> 00:32:10,028
We have to avoid death
during the operation at all costs.

463
00:32:10,528 --> 00:32:11,729
I won't let him die.

464
00:32:14,232 --> 00:32:15,867
I don't fail.

465
00:32:17,502 --> 00:32:19,704
- Keep him anesthetized.
- Will do.

466
00:32:23,274 --> 00:32:24,242
Monopolar.

467
00:32:27,645 --> 00:32:30,982
3rd assistant, hold here
while I detach the mesentery.

468
00:32:31,282 --> 00:32:32,116
Yes, ma'am.

469
00:32:35,520 --> 00:32:36,554
Forceps for intestines.

470
00:32:45,496 --> 00:32:46,664
We'll stop the bleeding.

471
00:32:46,798 --> 00:32:47,732
Monopolar.

472
00:32:51,402 --> 00:32:52,236
Here.

473
00:33:01,746 --> 00:33:03,748
I'll remove the recurred part. Metzen.

474
00:33:05,216 --> 00:33:06,117
- Forceps.
- Here.

475
00:33:14,025 --> 00:33:15,126
This knot.

476
00:33:16,227 --> 00:33:17,729
What about it?

477
00:33:18,262 --> 00:33:20,531
Just as I expected.

478
00:33:25,169 --> 00:33:27,438
Now conduct CHPP.

479
00:33:27,538 --> 00:33:29,207
Continuous hyperthermic
peritoneal perfusion?

480
00:33:29,340 --> 00:33:33,044
Warm 4L of saline solution
and cancer drug to 43C.

481
00:33:37,548 --> 00:33:39,917
Recirculate this for one hour
in the peritoneal cavity.

482
00:33:41,352 --> 00:33:45,623
What in the world are they doing?

483
00:33:45,757 --> 00:33:50,428
She's making the drug penetrate
the entire abdominal part

484
00:33:50,661 --> 00:33:53,431
before any adhesion occurs
after surgery.

485
00:33:53,564 --> 00:33:57,568
Since it's done when the least
number of cancer cells exist,

486
00:33:58,002 --> 00:34:01,072
it's very effective.

487
00:34:01,205 --> 00:34:06,010
I see.
So President Ninomiya will be saved?

488
00:34:07,045 --> 00:34:12,550
I never thought she'd succeed
in removing the entire peritoneum.

489
00:34:12,683 --> 00:34:16,754
No wonder you invited her to come.

490
00:34:17,021 --> 00:34:19,057
She has such outstanding skills.

491
00:34:19,190 --> 00:34:22,960
I wish she didn't butt in.

492
00:34:35,940 --> 00:34:37,442
Take this to the lab.

493
00:34:43,781 --> 00:34:45,750
Good job, Dr. Daimon.

494
00:34:46,584 --> 00:34:47,718
You too.

495
00:34:48,986 --> 00:34:50,088
It was outstanding.

496
00:34:56,861 --> 00:34:58,496
Removed the entire peritoneum?

497
00:34:59,530 --> 00:35:00,364
How?

498
00:35:02,600 --> 00:35:04,535
She did it in no time.

499
00:35:05,103 --> 00:35:06,070
It was a remarkable job.

500
00:35:06,771 --> 00:35:09,073
Ninomiya is in a stable condition.

501
00:35:10,374 --> 00:35:11,209
I see.

502
00:35:12,243 --> 00:35:14,312
That's good.

503
00:35:14,846 --> 00:35:18,382
The result of the lab
on the dissemination shows

504
00:35:19,484 --> 00:35:22,720
the differentiated adenocarcinoma,
same as the previous one.

505
00:35:27,358 --> 00:35:29,026
Does that mean that I'm the one

506
00:35:32,363 --> 00:35:35,500
who spread the cancer

507
00:35:36,701 --> 00:35:39,670
in the previous operation?

508
00:35:41,906 --> 00:35:48,412
Does that mean
Mr. Ninomiya had a recurrence?

509
00:35:49,580 --> 00:35:53,518
Rest assured all of us
in the 2nd surgery department

510
00:35:54,685 --> 00:35:55,953
will never speak about this.

511
00:35:57,021 --> 00:35:58,055
- Yes, sir.
- Yes, sir.

512
00:36:01,359 --> 00:36:07,765
I can't tell you how grateful
I am to have great men like you

513
00:36:09,367 --> 00:36:11,669
working for me.

514
00:36:11,802 --> 00:36:12,737
Professor Hiruma.

515
00:36:14,272 --> 00:36:17,975
The Hiruma Brand will live forever!

516
00:36:18,876 --> 00:36:22,380
Hooray! Hooray!

517
00:36:23,114 --> 00:36:24,348
- Ebina.
- Yes, sir.

518
00:36:26,551 --> 00:36:32,390
I'll do my best to help you
in the next chairperson election.

519
00:36:32,823 --> 00:36:33,658
I thank you, sir.

520
00:36:34,792 --> 00:36:38,229
Hooray! Hooray!

521
00:36:39,163 --> 00:36:41,566
Prof. Hiruma, you have a visitor.

522
00:36:41,632 --> 00:36:42,867
Did I have one scheduled?

523
00:36:44,769 --> 00:36:50,875
Thank you for choosing Daimon
as your fourth assistant today.

524
00:36:51,209 --> 00:36:53,277
Congratulations on your great work.

525
00:36:54,812 --> 00:36:57,381
- We should go now.
- See you later.

526
00:36:59,584 --> 00:37:00,518
This is a melon for you.

527
00:37:07,124 --> 00:37:09,694
- This is your bill.
- Bill?

528
00:37:15,333 --> 00:37:18,336
This one has two extra digits.

529
00:37:18,402 --> 00:37:19,670
There is no mistake.

530
00:37:22,873 --> 00:37:24,342
What a fool.

531
00:37:26,677 --> 00:37:32,016
What sort of fourth assistant
would receive three million yen?

532
00:37:32,083 --> 00:37:32,950
We have one who does.

533
00:37:34,785 --> 00:37:36,520
I think it's reasonable.

534
00:37:37,655 --> 00:37:40,925
You get all the credit for the surgery.

535
00:37:41,492 --> 00:37:46,063
And it includes the money to keep us quiet
about the mistake on the previous surgery.

536
00:37:46,430 --> 00:37:49,900
What are you talking about?

537
00:37:50,067 --> 00:37:53,638
Keep you quiet
about the previous surgery?

538
00:37:53,704 --> 00:37:56,440
My subordinates did that surgery.

539
00:37:56,507 --> 00:37:57,375
It was not so.

540
00:37:58,142 --> 00:38:02,513
Daimon told me
you performed the entire surgery.

541
00:38:02,580 --> 00:38:07,018
Michiko Daimon was not
present at the surgery.

542
00:38:07,151 --> 00:38:09,520
But she found out.

543
00:38:10,621 --> 00:38:15,026
It's the knots that remained
in Mr. Ninomiya's body.

544
00:38:16,060 --> 00:38:22,033
Depending on the habits of a surgeon,
various kinds of sutures exist.

545
00:38:22,166 --> 00:38:27,872
There are square knots, double knots,
and a combination of both.

546
00:38:28,506 --> 00:38:31,909
However, in Mr. Ninomiya's case,

547
00:38:31,976 --> 00:38:35,813
double knots, double knots,
and double knots.

548
00:38:35,880 --> 00:38:41,385
They were double knots all the way.

549
00:38:42,286 --> 00:38:45,289
This assured Daimon.

550
00:38:45,690 --> 00:38:48,092
Just as I expected.

551
00:38:48,326 --> 00:38:51,862
I heard you're good with a scalpel,

552
00:38:52,596 --> 00:38:55,633
but not so with knotting.

553
00:38:57,601 --> 00:39:02,139
You should watch your mouth.

554
00:39:02,873 --> 00:39:08,713
Either that,
or you really like the double knots.

555
00:39:12,116 --> 00:39:15,486
Please accept
the melon and the bill.

556
00:39:16,354 --> 00:39:20,324
I think the Hiruma Brand
will be secure now.

557
00:39:21,025 --> 00:39:25,029
Hooray! Hooray!

558
00:39:25,730 --> 00:39:26,697
Goodbye.

559
00:39:56,427 --> 00:39:57,261
Michiko.

560
00:39:58,028 --> 00:39:59,363
Good job.

561
00:40:00,531 --> 00:40:02,500
Surgery makes you hungry, huh?

562
00:40:02,566 --> 00:40:05,770
I can't decide between
the red beans or custard cream.

563
00:40:09,774 --> 00:40:11,442
- Excuse me.
- Welcome.

564
00:40:11,509 --> 00:40:13,811
- Can I have both?
- Thanks.

565
00:40:13,878 --> 00:40:17,281
I love you, Akira!

566
00:40:17,615 --> 00:40:18,449
Here you are.

567
00:40:21,685 --> 00:40:22,987
Thanks.

568
00:40:26,390 --> 00:40:29,560
Anyways,
Hiruma is such a cunning guy.

569
00:40:30,161 --> 00:40:33,431
He knew you'd never give up
once surgery starts.

570
00:40:33,497 --> 00:40:34,398
And he used you.

571
00:40:34,865 --> 00:40:38,803
He'd blame everything on you
if things went wrong.

572
00:40:39,370 --> 00:40:41,906
- No way.
- If not, he'll take the credit.

573
00:40:42,273 --> 00:40:45,042
If something went wrong,
he'd get rid of you.

574
00:40:45,476 --> 00:40:46,877
He's that kind of guy.

575
00:40:47,711 --> 00:40:49,513
But I'm feeling good today.

576
00:40:49,647 --> 00:40:56,220
Thanks to your dancing conference,
I could do a perfect operation!

577
00:40:56,287 --> 00:40:57,822
Thanks!

578
00:40:58,889 --> 00:40:59,857
Michiko.

579
00:41:00,958 --> 00:41:03,461
You're too nice as a surgeon.

580
00:41:20,177 --> 00:41:22,346
I was wrong to invite you.

581
00:41:22,813 --> 00:41:25,249
You don't run as I tell you.

582
00:41:25,316 --> 00:41:28,719
- I'm a surgeon, not a horse.
- You can leave now.

583
00:41:30,054 --> 00:41:34,391
If no one permits you to
do the operation, why stay?

584
00:41:36,794 --> 00:41:38,462
- Am I fired?
- Yep.

585
00:41:39,129 --> 00:41:40,865
I'm the one who called you,

586
00:41:42,099 --> 00:41:43,667
so I'm the one to fire you.

587
00:41:45,703 --> 00:41:50,441
My leg is much better now.

588
00:41:54,945 --> 00:41:56,447
You have great skills.

589
00:41:58,616 --> 00:41:59,683
This is too bad.

590
00:42:19,303 --> 00:42:22,740
The cancer had spread,
and the surgery was very tough.

591
00:42:23,173 --> 00:42:26,076
But Professor Hiruma was
able to remove it 100%.

592
00:42:26,777 --> 00:42:27,912
President Ninomiya.

593
00:42:28,712 --> 00:42:31,181
You're my important friend,

594
00:42:31,749 --> 00:42:33,150
and I need you to live a long life.

595
00:42:33,284 --> 00:42:36,487
You saved my life twice.

596
00:42:38,389 --> 00:42:40,758
I'm so grateful.

597
00:42:42,893 --> 00:42:46,497
Saeki. Hand it to me.

598
00:42:51,902 --> 00:42:53,070
Is this it, sir?

599
00:42:54,238 --> 00:42:57,341
Please don't worry about such a thing.

600
00:42:57,474 --> 00:43:00,144
It's a token of my appreciation.

601
00:43:00,277 --> 00:43:02,079
Please take it.

602
00:43:04,048 --> 00:43:05,583
Your appreciation.

603
00:43:06,483 --> 00:43:08,752
I shouldn't decline that.

604
00:43:10,187 --> 00:43:11,956
I thank you so much.

605
00:43:13,290 --> 00:43:17,595
You have great taste,
so I wonder what's in it.

606
00:43:22,132 --> 00:43:24,001
What a nice gift.

607
00:43:24,401 --> 00:43:27,004
A red scarf.

608
00:43:27,705 --> 00:43:29,506
It feels so soft.

609
00:43:29,974 --> 00:43:35,112
Oh, it's so warm.

610
00:43:36,313 --> 00:43:37,348
Excuse me.

611
00:43:39,249 --> 00:43:41,685
- Why are you here?
- You should knock.

612
00:43:42,019 --> 00:43:45,923
- To check on him after the surgery.
- After surgery?

613
00:43:47,858 --> 00:43:52,763
Have I seen this female doctor before?

614
00:43:52,896 --> 00:43:54,198
Me?

615
00:43:57,234 --> 00:43:58,168
During the surgery I...

616
00:43:58,235 --> 00:43:59,770
- Daimon!
- Shut up!

617
00:44:03,907 --> 00:44:06,043
Not worthy of introducing myself,

618
00:44:06,543 --> 00:44:08,112
but I'm Daimon, the fourth assistant.

619
00:44:09,313 --> 00:44:12,116
Right, you are the fourth assistant.

620
00:44:13,250 --> 00:44:14,385
She is a newcomer.

621
00:44:14,918 --> 00:44:18,489
We're sorry we all
suddenly started to talk loud.

622
00:44:20,491 --> 00:44:23,694
Daimon, let's have a meeting later.

623
00:44:24,361 --> 00:44:26,130
We'll take good care of you.

624
00:44:27,031 --> 00:44:29,433
Daimon. What do you want?

625
00:44:29,633 --> 00:44:32,236
Prof. Mabuchi just fired me.

626
00:44:32,770 --> 00:44:33,604
I see.

627
00:44:34,171 --> 00:44:36,807
I'll take you back.

628
00:44:37,641 --> 00:44:40,277
I will hire you.

629
00:44:41,478 --> 00:44:45,883
And what is your purpose
for wanting to work in the hospital?

630
00:44:46,717 --> 00:44:49,787
Status? Prestige? Money?

631
00:44:51,155 --> 00:44:53,023
- All of them?
- I don't want any of them.

632
00:44:54,291 --> 00:44:55,959
- Then what?
- Many operations.

633
00:44:56,794 --> 00:44:57,928
Many operations?

634
00:44:58,062 --> 00:44:59,897
Let me do
as many operations as possible.

635
00:45:03,133 --> 00:45:04,368
Okay, I understand.

636
00:45:04,735 --> 00:45:06,937
Operate as many as you like.

637
00:45:08,439 --> 00:45:11,075
I will not be her assistant.

638
00:45:12,409 --> 00:45:14,478
- Me neither.
- Me neither.

639
00:45:15,079 --> 00:45:17,848
Dang it, that's the problem.

640
00:45:19,316 --> 00:45:20,384
I'll settle for you.

641
00:45:23,921 --> 00:45:25,322
Nobody wants to do it.

642
00:45:26,223 --> 00:45:29,193
Be Daimon's assistant
when she does an operation.

643
00:45:31,095 --> 00:45:31,929
Yes, sir.

644
00:45:32,563 --> 00:45:37,634
Daimon, starting today,
you'll be soaked in surgery.

645
00:45:39,069 --> 00:45:41,038
- Good luck.
- I can't wait.

646
00:45:45,275 --> 00:45:47,377
Oh, by the way,

647
00:45:49,179 --> 00:45:52,783
should you make any mistakes,

648
00:45:53,417 --> 00:45:57,354
we won't have anything to do
with it at all. Be aware of it.

649
00:45:58,622 --> 00:46:00,023
I don't fail.

650
00:46:03,327 --> 00:46:04,228
Did you hear that?

651
00:46:05,462 --> 00:46:07,564
She doesn't fail.

652
00:46:11,068 --> 00:46:12,603
She doesn't fail!

653
00:46:18,208 --> 00:46:20,778
Dr. Daimon, please do a good job.

654
00:46:27,718 --> 00:46:30,621
Begin surgery
to remove a tumor from the colon.

655
00:46:30,854 --> 00:46:31,688
Scalpel.

656
00:46:32,756 --> 00:46:35,325
<i>She hates groups</i>
<i>and being controlled.</i>

657
00:46:36,794 --> 00:46:41,298
<i>Her medical certifications</i>
<i>and work experience are her only weapons.</i>

658
00:46:42,866 --> 00:46:44,768
<i>Surgeon Michiko Daimon,</i>

659
00:46:46,703 --> 00:46:50,841
<i>also known as Doctor-X.</i>

660
00:46:52,543 --> 00:46:54,812
A viper and a mongoose?

661
00:46:54,878 --> 00:46:56,680
I'll never be treated by a surgeon.

662
00:46:56,814 --> 00:46:58,949
Exchange the intestine and kidney.

663
00:46:59,082 --> 00:47:00,918
We may lose both professors' wives.

664
00:47:01,051 --> 00:47:02,653
I can't stop the bleeding.

665
00:47:02,786 --> 00:47:03,954
Both are demoted?

666
00:47:04,054 --> 00:47:05,422
I'll take care of you.

667
00:47:05,489 --> 00:47:07,391
I won't help you get promoted.
